      <activity id="b16688a0-4929-5d76-90ff-b11d4bc34f52" activityNameId="b2374d3c-ae34-5fd6-af48-ee9fb3091562" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, helicopter, twin-engine, LTO cycle</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, helicopter, twin-engine, LTO cycle
One take-over and landing of an helikopter, using specific LTO emission factors for a Airbus Helicopters EC 135 VIP helicopter provided of the federal office of civil aviation (FOCCA);
UUID: 71ecba42-4d7a-33f3-84ad-742e70986cf1
This dataset describes the energy requirements and emissions of a Landing-and-Take-Over (LTO) Cycle of a helicopter.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Data is for an average Swiss helicopter for freight transport (6500kg) using kerosene
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: 0LTO
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_71ecba42-4d7a-33f3-84ad-742e70986cf1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
